# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Wrangler
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .wrangler/ holds the LOCAL D1 SQLite file and dev state. It is machine-local
# scratch data, never the source of truth -- the schema in migrations/ is.
.wrangler/

# Local secrets for `wrangler dev`. Must never be committed.
# .dev.vars.example is the exception: it lists the NAMES with no values, so a
# developer knows what to set. The negation must come after the wildcard.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
!.dev.vars.example

# Wrangler 3 reads .dev.vars; Wrangler 4 and most other tooling read .env.
# Neither was covered before, and a secret only has to be committable once.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database exports / backups
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backups taken from the app's Settings -> Export Data, or from
# `wrangler d1 export`, contain real customer names, phone numbers, addresses
# and the full financial ledger. Keep them out of the repository.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
backup*.sql
taqwa-export-*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
